  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "tone-definition",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-tone-mapping",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0682d4015b96"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0682d4015b96",
          "exact": "Tone mapping is a technique used in image processing and computer graphics to map one set of colors to another to approximate the appearance of high-dynamic-range (HDR) images in a medium that has a more limited dynamic range."
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "目标引文在 [78,110) 处明确表述 \"map one set of colors to another\"，对应 claim 的\"把一组颜色映射到另一组\"；在 [111,226) 处表述 \"to approximate the appearance of high-dynamic-range (HDR) images in a medium that has a more limited dynamic range\"，对应 claim 的\"在动态范围更有限的媒介上近似显示 HDR 图像外观\"；[0,4) 处 \"Tone\" 对应\"色调映射（Tone mapping）\"，\"technique\" 对应\"技术\"。claim 为引文的忠实中文转述，无实质增益、无遗漏关键限定，故判定 supported。注：rationale_offsets 的字符区间基于提供的 evidence quote 文本计算（请求中未提供源文章全文，无法对源全文另行定位）。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-tone-mapping",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0682d4015b96",
          "start": 78,
          "end": 110
        },
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-tone-mapping",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0682d4015b96",
          "start": 111,
          "end": 226
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0682d4015b96",
          "subject": "Tone mapping",
          "predicate": "is defined as",
          "object": "a technique to map one set of colors to another to approximate the appearance of HDR images in a medium with a more limited dynamic range"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "tone-local-ops",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-tone-mapping",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-cb52956d0035"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-cb52956d0035",
          "exact": "Local (or spatially varying) operators: the parameters of the non-linear function change in each pixel, according to features extracted from the surrounding parameters. In other words, the effect of the algorithm changes in each pixel according to the local features of the image. Those algorithms are more complicated than the global ones; they can show artifacts (e.g. halo effect and ringing); and the output can look unrealistic, but they can (if used correctly) provide the best performance, since human vision is mainly sensitive to local contrast."
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文在 [40,103) 处表述 \"the parameters of the non-linear function change in each pixel, according to features extracted from the surrounding parameters\"，并在 [169,280) 处重申 \"changes in each pixel according to the local features of the image\"，对应 claim 的\"非线性函数参数随像素局部特征逐像素变化\"；[281,340) 处 \"more complicated than the global ones\" 对应\"比全局算子复杂\"；[341,396) 处 \"artifacts (e.g. halo effect and ringing)\" 对应\"可能产生 halo（光晕）与振铃伪影\"；[434,496) 与 [497,554) 处 \"they can (if used correctly) provide the best performance, since human vision is mainly sensitive to local contrast\" 对应\"能提供最佳性能——因为人眼主要对局部对比敏感\"。claim 省略了原文 \"if used correctly\" 的使用条件限定，但 claim 使用模态词\"能\"（can）而非全称断言，未超出原文断言范围，且核心因果（since human vision is mainly sensitive to local contrast）完整保留，故判定 supported。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
